16T21:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4d7d656b331745b1f2dd2979cabc6664b362b3b4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4d7d656b331745b1f2dd2979cabc6664b362b3b4.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 16 at 7:24PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 724 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from 7 miles southeast of Prewitt Reservoir\nto 6 miles northwest of Gary, or extending from 13 miles north of\nAkron to 11 miles southeast of Fort Morgan, moving southeast at 15\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nAkron, Midway, Gary and Fremont Butte.","ends":"2026-08-16T20:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Morgan County; Washington County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d9651bc26a27ad7c4caea82bf390cee779147b0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3d9651bc26a27ad7c4caea82bf390cee779147b0.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 16 at 6:45PM MDT until August 16 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Logan County in northeastern Colorado...\nCentral Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nNorth Central Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 645 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has\nfallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nBeaver Creek, Pawnee Creek, Bijou Creek, Wildcat Creek, Badger\nCreek, Kiowa Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch\nare expected over the area. This additional rain will result in\nminor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFort Morgan, Brush, Wiggins, Log Lane Village, Merino, Hillrose,\nSnyder, Prewitt Reservoir, Fort Morgan Airport, Union and Messex.","ends":"2026-08-16T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56abaf26c235284d9caf2a8d5c5a3bb3400a5848.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.56abaf26c235284d9caf2a8d5c5a3bb3400a5848.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-17T00:07:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 170007 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 607 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Showers and storms continue this evening, some strong to severe. Strong winds, hail, and heavy rain/flash flooding on the table. - Afternoon storms are expected again on Monday, mostly over the eastern mountains and Raton Mesa. - A bit drier through the rest of th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-16T17:21:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 161721 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1121 AM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-171730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-16T18:35:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... No meteorological fire weather concerns across the district